#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096382 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "b77c065c-3821-513c-9376-6e7108074616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4701" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/49df59f984403cbbc994361c96313eca4d0875a7030dd997c90f1e393e23b69c.png)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/dded05f0961034de6808d8f91f64afe8c367cec3c11fafdb26946090fa9c0891.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096383 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/id #uuid "7760b6ce-91fb-5ba6-beb2-c244d6a73d69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4702" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/0c3483f97994da22dc0c739f9c3a26f87e070d28b684e63955a1129d00f9c755.png)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/9f1beb75e17aabdbeb5d814ae7ce3018f2ea89c36211070d40060d57445ca936.png)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/84de3f5eddf0a05d4f2d69aebd1537feb23a228fba3e1af31678dd4bdb1b59df.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ebf0657-4d78-56b5-bc74-4d6bc0c5e774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,6,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374523} {:answer/id #uuid "5e44dfbf-d02b-5a54-9aa0-a085019bdd61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,6,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374524} {:answer/id #uuid "11707825-b7d1-526d-a0ca-83315a9b9953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374525} {:answer/id #uuid "4d0fbf33-cdc4-5298-bc6b-877279fbd179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374526} {:answer/id #uuid "a34f2682-c1ea-5c34-9310-eb89c305ab31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11707825-b7d1-526d-a0ca-83315a9b9953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨17,14,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374525} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cdfc3bd-fdca-5559-ad69-5b8738763495" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "431a8c5f-b48a-570a-b528-7d3773d13396" :question/math-academy-id "q-130926" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+z=-3 \\\\  & y-2z=-2 \\\\  & z=8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=8$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-2(8)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-2+16=14.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=14$ and $z=8$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(14)+(8)=-3\\,⟹\\,x=17.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=17,y=14$, and $z=8.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨17,14,8⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84826572-6121-5e20-abb0-c418ae03d84c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374530} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6e9369-3da4-5641-a4c0-d99cd4fac697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374531} {:answer/id #uuid "ea994afe-e536-5771-836e-e1cf5147e33f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374532} {:answer/id #uuid "54858800-49a2-5458-87db-995e511b467e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374533} {:answer/id #uuid "91dd7ea8-b7de-5ce9-b1de-3791eb3ced3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84826572-6121-5e20-abb0-c418ae03d84c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374530} :answer-field/id #uuid "59ced7c4-89a1-5c1d-b82e-60536562e135" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59d8291a-54d6-53ae-b0c1-56a672117493" :question/math-academy-id "q-130928" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{7}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "819dcbf3-244b-56f3-bac9-c3460d9a6b07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=6$ and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374537} {:answer/id #uuid "333ab59b-93f1-5fba-9c9b-4b5d12fb6180" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=8$ and $z=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374538} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6ffb27-91bf-5103-93ac-3c2f05784d25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=2$ and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374539} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf448e5-07e9-53c1-aa13-a28d056b96a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=4$ and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374540} {:answer/id #uuid "58f54120-1c2e-507f-983f-67c68f6007e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=5$ and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff6ffb27-91bf-5103-93ac-3c2f05784d25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,y=2$ and $z=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374539} :answer-field/id #uuid "12ccae99-0e09-5930-8e41-6f2ecc09369d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5bd93618-ca8f-501f-8ec1-14f3febe4ba6" :question/math-academy-id "q-20263" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=6 \\\\  & y+z=5 \\\\  & 2x+3y+2z=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and hence solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 14\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=6 \\\\  & y+z=5 \\\\  & z=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=3$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(3)=5\\,⟹\\,y=5-3=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=2$ and $z=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(2)+(3)=6\\,⟹\\,x=6-5=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1,y=2$ and $z=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "833a74c7-6a79-5b27-a262-23c25afa7527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307022} {:answer/id #uuid "b619c9e5-c442-5bc2-8bde-f43426aa74c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307023} {:answer/id #uuid "1fc543af-5aa8-552e-9550-b2e0855a2ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307024} {:answer/id #uuid "2f93a8f4-ba16-5259-a528-5852d97cbf7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307025} {:answer/id #uuid "4fe989b6-caa2-5cd6-aba3-7fbbcf3a9f7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b619c9e5-c442-5bc2-8bde-f43426aa74c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307023} :answer-field/id #uuid "40bca7a6-a706-5791-91b5-fe08bcd75d2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ebe05898-9b62-5489-8bf9-f004db945a43" :question/math-academy-id "q-20524" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 6 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaf3f51d-993b-5a8f-8ac3-503bb81c8598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374544} {:answer/id #uuid "079894a4-0c93-599d-a3a4-978c52a381c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374545} {:answer/id #uuid "405807de-c8b0-5abd-8e09-6ffb76f08294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374546} {:answer/id #uuid "c7fbe680-5bd8-5caf-b8b8-59a998f8b885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374547} {:answer/id #uuid "60232ded-5c74-541a-b184-08142201701d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "405807de-c8b0-5abd-8e09-6ffb76f08294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374546} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcc615b3-84ae-50db-89d9-e7a47be03e54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8debf20-bfaf-5a47-b96d-4adce3d312bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-20533" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=0 \\\\  & y+2z=0 \\\\  & x+y+3z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11399a01-b35a-5641-b37b-c3d969a5abd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374551} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f93267-dc2c-54c2-8cc7-0f2c835ad818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374552} {:answer/id #uuid "3b5e9194-5c6f-565b-b7be-541cf9c8b342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374553} {:answer/id #uuid "344942a2-a52d-5f61-a683-427bc12b2e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374554} {:answer/id #uuid "bf946d7e-2314-5cbb-82be-974b93c1f91a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3f93267-dc2c-54c2-8cc7-0f2c835ad818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374552} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaf96bbd-80c0-5d06-882c-0625937ad172" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b0ab2ea-5bc8-5361-b6e4-ca31cdf1350a" :question/math-academy-id "q-20539" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 9 & -13 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 9 & -13 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 17 & -26\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab1df4f7-b683-58f9-9a53-9ab3b8f3de6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 5$, and $z = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095972} {:answer/id #uuid "d48de23d-197f-5638-8f67-022bd20311ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y =-5$, and $z = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095973} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4aec20-6490-5d49-b934-a54e24f45880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 6$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095974} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b2100b-3e34-5897-a886-74eaa7dc84ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x =-1$, $y = 2$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095975} {:answer/id #uuid "3759267e-7f9c-5109-a8da-b96bba06dc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 1$, $y =-6$, and $z =-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef4aec20-6490-5d49-b934-a54e24f45880" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x = 4$, $y = 6$, and $z = 5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095974} :answer-field/id #uuid "a873c750-ef0d-5d9f-b3a2-06f31ec27870" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cdba1d21-3eaf-575a-9b38-07c8181fcd34" :question/math-academy-id "q-73396" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=8 \\\\  & -2x+2y-3z=-11 \\\\  & x+z=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z=8 \\\\ y-z=1 \\\\ z=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5)=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5)=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b44ac0b-f0a6-5169-91fa-ccd943551ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-17,12,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307050} {:answer/id #uuid "24bf5c93-01a8-5636-94b1-c4ee5dc208b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,-8,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307051} {:answer/id #uuid "fdbf2bac-e66d-5284-aee3-3749274a9cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307052} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d5d5c5-0faa-553d-8841-fbb325465107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307053} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ec3980-8f7f-5956-9395-d25572148fdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨25,-18,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdbf2bac-e66d-5284-aee3-3749274a9cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨39,-28,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307052} :answer-field/id #uuid "e845c512-1717-5897-a5f6-26fcd9cc631e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2165c009-aa54-51cd-9ee0-62e80fd9ad16" :question/math-academy-id "q-73584" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y-2z=3 \\\\ y+5z=-8 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+5(4)=-8\\,⟹\\,y=-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-28$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(-28)-2(4)=3\\,⟹\\,x=39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=39$, $y=-28$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form $⟨39,-28,4⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b48e0c1c-325f-52cd-ac4a-b25020518dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374558} {:answer/id #uuid "97f22f48-ddb6-51f9-9703-e661ea10f060" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374559} {:answer/id #uuid "cf25bdf3-6542-5902-8fee-06fb1e09ae82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨52,21,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374560} {:answer/id #uuid "b7436d5e-ec50-5709-bc99-8be3c8388500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374561} {:answer/id #uuid "6c195b8c-e4f3-57a4-abc0-a09a3e393d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48e0c1c-325f-52cd-ac4a-b25020518dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-58,-23,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374558} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca320e6-dbd6-531e-9ffd-17421d507126" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a8b2c9f-398c-5dbe-9647-f240ec1722c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-73588" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 16 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z=-2 \\\\ y+2z=-1 \\\\ z=11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=11$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(11)=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-23$ and $z=11$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-23)+3(11)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-58.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-58$, $y=-23$, and $z=11.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-58,-23,11⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374563 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b82a4316-8170-5595-9fee-5ae32b156a1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374565} {:answer/id #uuid "33dc155f-6682-5a1f-8e71-3176597d12d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374566} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1a9344-4774-54e2-baac-6bdfa344bf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374567} {:answer/id #uuid "b4260d06-8943-5ddb-b6ef-c5b2eac2aa80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374568} {:answer/id #uuid "be73c87c-691d-5498-a59c-2991ff6f1c30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33dc155f-6682-5a1f-8e71-3176597d12d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374566} :answer-field/id #uuid "be25a1a3-304d-585b-b387-dfe618b092f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2d0c5e25-563c-570e-8ef3-6aa05d25d8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73592" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-6y+3z=-6 \\\\  & 2x-4y+3z=-1 \\\\  & 2y-4z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
